 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Japan built an entire airport on an island it made in the sea.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Under the seabed was about twenty meters of soft clay, mostly water.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Engineers pushed about a million sand drains into it, to squeeze the water out.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then they piled millions of tons of rock and dirt on top.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "The clay squeezed, and the whole island sank.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "By 1999, it had sunk more than eight meters. Way more than planned.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So the terminal stands on columns that can be adjusted.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "When one corner sinks, they lift that column, and slide in steel plates.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Now you know. What should we explain next?",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
